      "notes": [
        "British Columbia's annual return uses the legislated 5.60% lowest rate and a $690 basic reduction. January–June 2026 payroll tables use 5.06% and a $575 reduction; July–December payroll uses a 6.14% prorated rate and an $805 reduction.",
        "Manitoba's annual brackets are the CRA return table ($47,564 / $101,200). The January 2026 T4127 payroll tables still use $47,000 / $100,000.",
        "Newfoundland and Labrador's annual basic personal amount used here is $13,094. Payroll withholding used $11,188 until July 2026 and a prorated $15,000 after that.",
        "Provincial and territorial dividend tax credits are not in this dataset. Dividend results omit them and say so.",
        "Quebec deduction for workers is the lesser of 6 percent of employment income and the year's maximum. It is not applied to self-employment, pensions or investment income.",
        "Self-employed CPP/QPP is not calculated. Employment income is the only income that creates CPP, EI, QPP and QPIP in these estimates."
      ],
